course: dictionary
lesson: 12176
title: Conclude: decide, or end
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word conclude has three meanings, and the sentence around it shows which one you need. Look for clues such as «that», «with», or «the final part». «The results show the plant needs light, so Sam concluded that light helps plants grow.» Here conclude means to decide something is true after thinking about the facts.
explain: When a sentence says «The concert concluded with a song everyone knew», conclude means to come to an end. The song was the last thing that happened. «To conclude» at the start of a sentence means you are about to give the final part of a talk or a piece of writing.
explain: Conclude can also mean to arrange something finally, such as a deal. «The two companies concluded the deal after three long meetings» means they finally agreed it. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: To conclude means to decide that something is true after thinking about the facts.
fact: To conclude means to end, or to come to an end.
fact: To conclude an agreement means to arrange it finally.
fact: A «conclusion» is the last part of a report, where you say what the results show.
fact: Common phrases: «conclude that», «to conclude», «concluded with».

exercise: «After the experiment, Sam concluded that the plant needs light to grow.» What does concluded mean here? | Forgot the answer | Argued loudly with a friend | Ended the game early | *Decided something is true after thinking about the facts
exercise: «The concert concluded with a song everyone knew.» What does concluded mean here? | Was cancelled | *Came to an end | Started and began | Got louder
exercise: «In her science report, Mia wrote a clear conclusion at the end.» Which word names the last part of a report? | title | introduction | *conclusion | experiment
test: «To conclude, the class agreed to plant more trees.» What does To conclude mean in this sentence? | To start the first part | To forget the plan | To shout the answer | *To start the final part
test: «The two companies concluded the deal after three long meetings.» What does concluded the deal mean? | Asked for a deal | Broke the deal | *Arranged the agreement finally | Lost the papers
exam: «From the facts, Ben can conclude that it will rain today.» What does can conclude mean? | Wish that it would stop | Ask his mum for an umbrella | *Decide it is likely true from the facts | Draw a picture of the clouds
